{% extends "layout.njk" %}

{% block content %}
<section class="card">
  <h1>About this example</h1>
  <p>
    This page has no <code>load()</code> function: it measures the pure Nunjucks
    render path (layout inheritance, helpers, compression, security headers).
  </p>
  <h2>Features covered</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>File-based SSR pages with companion loaders and dynamic <code>[slug]</code> params</li>
    <li>File-based JSON API with Zod schemas and named middleware</li>
    <li>ORM models (<code>zdb</code>), relations, eager loading, soft deletes, query cache, migrations</li>
    <li>Services with validation, ACID transactions, memoization and timeouts</li>
    <li>Native JWT authentication and rate limiting</li>
    <li>Background jobs, domain events and listeners</li>
    <li>Compression, payload limits, health probes, metrics, CORS and redirects</li>
  </ul>
</section>
{% endblock %}

